{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And her flow shall be upon him.</b> One might think it is reckoned to her period — that if he lay with her on the fifth day of her flow, he would be impure only three days like her — therefore Scripture says ״וְטָמֵא שִׁבְעַת יָמִים״. And what does ״וּתְהִי נִדָּתָהּ עָלָיו״ teach? Just as she imparts impurity to a person and to clay vessels, so too he imparts impurity to a person and to clay vessels (Sifra; Niddah 33)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:06:38.827542597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}